{"title":"News publisher files class action antitrust suit against Google, citing AI’s harms to their bottom line (TechCrunch, 2023-12-15T17:56:02+00:00)","text":"News publisher files class action antitrust suit against Google, citing AI’s harms to their bottom line (TechCrunch, 2023-12-15T17:56:02+00:00)
A new class action lawsuit filed this week in the U.S. District Court in D.C. accuses Google and parent company Alphabet of anticompetitive behavior in violation of U.S. antitrust law, the Sherman Act, and others, on behalf of news publishers. The case, filed by Arkansas-based publisher Helena World Chronicle, argues that Google “siphons off” news publishers’ content, their readers and ad revenue through anticompetitive means. It also specifically cites new AI technologies like Google’s Search Generative Experience (SGE) and Bard AI chatbot as worsening the problem.

In the complaint, Helena World Chronicle, which owns and publishes two weekly newspapers in Arkansas, argues that Google is “starving the free press” by sharing publishers’ content on Google, losing them “billions of dollars.”

In addition to new AI technologies, the suit points to Google’s older question-and-answer technologies, like the “Knowledge Graph” launched in May 2012, as part of the problem.","entities":["Alphabet","Helena World Chronicle","U.S. District Court in D.C.","Search Generative Experience","Bard AI chatbot","Knowledge Graph","anticompetitive behavior","U.S. antitrust law","Sherman Act","Arkansas","question-and-answer technologies","News publisher files class action antitrust suit against Google, citing AI’s harms to their bottom line","class action lawsuit","TechCrunch","AI technologies"],"facts":["A comprehensive list of 2023 tech layoffs -MENTIONS-> Alphabet","Earnings week ahead: Amazon, Microsoft, Alphabet, Meta, Ford, GM and more -MENTIONS-> Alphabet","ASX set to rise ahead of inflation report after big tech lifts Wall Street -MENTIONS-> Alphabet","Amazon’s Tye Brady discusses generative AI, humanoid robots and mobile manipulation -MENTIONS-> Alphabet","Palestine’s growing tech industry has been literally blown apart by Israel’s war on Hamas -MENTIONS-> Alphabet"]}
